```

Perhaps some devices _always_ have `event.getSource() == InputDevice.SOURCE_CLASS_NONE`? For me, at least, it would be useful to totally ignore this input source, since I **never** intend to skip to the end of a podcast, while skipping forward and backwards a few seconds is something I do very frequently.

```
                if(UserPreferences.shouldHardwareButtonSkip()) {
                    endPlayback(true);
                } else {
                    // regardless of the source of the skip command,
                    // user actually wants to fast-forward
                    seekDelta(UserPreferences.getFastFowardSecs() * 1000);
                }
```

Perhaps the two-way toggle could be changed to a three way option to support this?

```
->  (1) Hardware buttons always skips to next episode
        current behavior of [X]
    (2) Bluetooth media buttons fast-forward, others skip to next episodes.
        current behavior of [ ]
    (3) Hardware buttons always fast-forwards
        new option
```

